  "result": "Done — gate verdict **`OK`** on the first of six runs (`3 witnesses, 2 names, reads 2 atom(s)`).\n\n**The body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/reverse_travel.lean`): the component of the velocity along the direction the body points, written as the scalar product of `kin_velocity` with the (Core-normalised) `kin_heading` over the `x` and `y` selectors, compared `.le` against `.neg (.param \"reverse_speed_tolerance\")` — exactly the contract's \"at most the negative of the reverse speed tolerance\". `kin.speed` and `kin.gear` are not read, as the record's justification directs; no duration, place or signal enters it. `narrowings := []`: the strictness and the sign are both dictated by the contract's words, and the heading's normalisation is Core's reading of the atom, noted in the header rather than claimed as a choice.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/reverse_travel.lean`): one car pointing east over three instants a second apart, tolerance 0.2 m/s; `holds` moves 1.5 m/s west (component −1.5), `fails` 1.5 m/s east (+1.5), `blind` repeats the reversing manoeuvre with `kin.velocity` masked. No structures or devices — the concept reads neither, so the parking bay lives in the motion only.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory with the run log, the figures I chose, and why I stopped.",
